  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "in an udumbara fruit; उदुम्बरमशक, उदुम्बरकृमि &c. are proverbial",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "expressions like कूपमण्डूक meaning ‘any useless person.’",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 25. गालिमन्तः—मत् expresses निन्दा ( because nothing bet-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ter can be expected of you). शशकविषाण—see Nîti. S'a. sl. 5.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 26. महाराम—आराम means a garden, but more probably",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "here ‘delight, pleasure; his path is full of delight because he is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "free from all desire. चर्मन्—( 1 ) bark; ( 2 ) skin. सुखैः &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Mr. Telang says—“The result is the same with what are called",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "pleasures or with sorrows; i. e. whether I am in worldy affluence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "or otherwise, I get food and clothing in one case as in the other.’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "But सुख and दुःख here seem to refer to the two courses of life",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "marked out, viz. that of happily living on alms and worshipping",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "S'iva or that of living a miserable life of sycophany and hu-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "mouring rich men. सदृश—should better be rendered by ‘similar’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "than by ‘the same’. The result, viz. obtaining food and clothing",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "is similar in both cases but not the same as the one is full of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "happiness, the other attended by misery. त्रिनेत्रं, ०मदान्ध—mark",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "the contrast suggested by these words.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 27. करटिनः—i. e. elephants belonging to the enemy.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "The meaning of the first line is-We did not distinguish our-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "selves as successful warriors. Cf. l. 2. Sl. 47. नितम्ब०-निबद्धफलके",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "v. l. the boardlike i. e. expansive and fleshy or well-rounded",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "( निबद्ध ) hips. झणत्झाङ्कार–a tautological expression; झणत् and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "झांकार meaning the same thing. For the idea comp. स्थाने स्थाने",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मुखरककुभो झांकृतैर्निर्झराणाम् ’ Uttar. II. 14. पयः—the reading वयः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "makes no sense. The fourth line is the same as that of sl. 48.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Additional Sl.—बली—A demon; his story is too well known to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the Hindu students to require any notice here; see A. Dictionary.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "व्याधयः—i. e. the diseases in the world. We did not free the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "people from the diseases humanity is heir to. Mr. Telang who",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "reads the last line as ०मानगणनां मिथ्या वहन्न लज्जसे remarks.—‘The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "stanza occurs in the Mahánàtaka. The last line is not metrical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "as it stands. In the Mahànátaka it runs thus—चेतः सा पुरुषाभि",
          "end": "join"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
